WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:07.340
Plaiting or plating is a technique that
uses two strands of yarn held together.

2
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.860
The machine positions the yarn in such

3
00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.620
a way that the strands are knitted
together at the same time,

4
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:19.060
but one strand shows on the purl side,
the other strand shows on the knit side.

5
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.700
Keep in mind that you're knitting two
strands together, so you'll want to use

6
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.060
a finer yarn than you might
normally use on your machine.

7
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.140
Also, mixing weights and textures of yarn

8
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.540
can produce very interesting
plaiting results.

9
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.020
In this plaiting example,

10
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.500
the teal is showing on the purl side and
the white is showing on the knit side.

11
00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.460
Think of the possibilities of having

12
00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:53.140
reversible fabric, color wise.
Without using a plaiting yarn feeder.

13
00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.380
The yarns would normally twist

14
00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:01.200
and the colors would randomly be
shown on each side of the knitting.

15
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.660
To knit in plaiting on Brother standard
gauge machines,

16
00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:13.200
we need to replace the yarn feeder
assembly that's in the sinker plate.

17
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.380
Remove the sinker plate from the machine.

18
00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.050
Loosen and remove the screws
holding the assembly.

19
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.380
If they're tight, use a screwdriver
or a coin to loosen them.

20
00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:32.040
With the screws removed,
carefully slip the yarn feeder out

21
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:43.400
and insert the plating feeder
and secure it with the screws.

22
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.140
To thread the feeder,
snap one yarn into the back slot

23
00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:53.240
and insert the other
strand in the front slot.

24
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.340
The feeder positions the yarns so they

25
00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:03.210
align in a way that one strand is held
in front and shows on the purl side.

26
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.980
The other strand shows on the knit side.

27
00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:14.280
Plaiting can also be done with the ribber
using a ribber plaiting attachment.

28
00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.100
Don't forget, since you're knitting

29
00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:20.320
with two strands, you'll need to use finer
yarn than you might normally knit with.

